# v1.17 — mask the root's MISSION COMPLETE shut on DEFEND/DENY roots.
#
# Owner's decision, 2026-08-10. DEFEND/DENY roots stop being COMPLETABLE: the
# horizon no longer opens the root's DONE bit. ENDEX is untouched and keeps
# firing on every success — that combination is the whole point, and it is only
# available because v1.16 split `root_may_declare_the_end` (which act closes the
# window) from `command_closes_the_operation` (who announces it). v1.13 masked
# the claim shut and lost the announcement with it, because they were ONE
# predicate.
#
# ── why the claim goes ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The claim buys nothing operationally. Early close is bounded at
# `grace_window` = 12 steps by construction, and the terminal speed bonus keys
# on `_success_step` rather than on the close step, so closing early pays no
# speed bonus at all. At N=100 the measured difference between claim+ENDEX and
# ENDEX-only episodes is p = 0.9942 (defend_brique_v13/final, Mann-Whitney,
# refs #33 §3).
#
# Its informational value is negative in practice: `defend_brique` files 321
# root claims at 0.71 false.
#
# And pricing cannot fix it. Three independent experiments, three scenarios,
# two root types:
#
#   lever                       run                  effect
#   done_false -2.0             squad_v9             266 claims -> 0 (silence)
#   root_done_bonus first-only  defend_brique_v12    321 claims -> 0 (silence)
#   done_false -0.5             defend_brique_v11/13 spam at 0.44-0.71 false
#
# Every price moves claim VOLUME without moving claim INFORMEDNESS. The
# announcement, meanwhile, is free and guaranteed — 391/391 under v1.16 — so
# masking the claim costs no observability.
#
# ── the change ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `missions.is_completable` reverts to plain COMPLETABLE membership;
# HORIZON_COMPLETABLE and the `defend_horizon` parameter are deleted rather than
# left as a knob that does nothing. `ScenarioSpec.defend_horizon` is unchanged
# and still adjudicates DEFEND success — it is an adjudication clause only now.
#
# NOT rollout-neutral, and by more than the mask: `root_may_declare_the_end` is
# defined by the same predicate, so v1.13's SITREP early-close route reactivates
# with it. A root SITREP at or after T0 now closes the grace window and collects
# `root_done_bonus`, which is what keeps that reward from becoming dead on a
# defense (the v1.4 failure). Measured perturbation on the incumbent policies is
# recorded in the ROADMAP entry for this cycle.
#
# Spaces FROZEN: Discrete(228)/Box(220) — masking only. The whole fleet loads.
#
# ── controls: v13 / v18 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `defend_brique_v13` and `fireteam_defend_v18` are the controls: same budgets,
# same seed, same reward overrides, claim OPEN. One variable.
#
# ── what to watch ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `successes_announced` — the bar is complete, 391/391 at N=100 seed 123 under
# v1.16. Anything short of complete is the finding, because it would mean the
# split predicate did not hold and masking the claim took the announcement with
# it a second time.
#
# Then: root claims are 0 BY CONSTRUCTION (assert `done_admissible_root` is 0
# too, or the silence is unattributable); `closed_on_root_report_rate` should be
# carried by SITREPs rather than claims; and no reward path may silently vanish
# — `root_done_bonus` must still be collected on the episodes that close early.
defend_brique_v14    --scenario defend_brique   --total-steps 3000000 --seed 12 --reward defend_survivor_scale=0.35 --reward root_done_bonus_first_claim_only=false
fireteam_defend_v19  --scenario fireteam_defend --total-steps 3500000 --seed 12 --reward defend_survivor_scale=0.35 --reward root_done_bonus_first_claim_only=false
